--TEST--
A Core\Cli\Live handle refuses to paint once the region it names has closed -- `rule:tooling/terminal-output-is-a-sink` sections 5 and 8
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Answering the handle is the one way to get one out of the call that made it,
// which is what makes `rule:tooling/in-place-output-is-a-scoped-live-region`'s scoping reachable from source at all: the
// region ends with the `live` call, and a handle outliving it names a region
// that is no longer there.
var $escaped = Core\Cli::live(fn(Core\Cli\Live $live): Core\Cli\Live => {
    $live->set([Core\Cli\Text::plain("while it is open")]);
    return $live;
});
try {
    $escaped->set([Core\Cli\Text::plain("after it closed")]);
    echo "painted\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
Core\Cli\Live::set(): this handle's region has closed, or an inner one is open inside it — a live region is scoped to the `Core\Cli::live` call that made it, and only the innermost open region paints
